messages.reasoning_content:
`ghPaginated` throws on non-zero exit — but the aggregation read needs the exit-code guard (the "undetermined" notice path), so it can't use ghPaginated directly without a try/catch, which is fine — wrap in try/catch and return the `withNotice(... {kind:"undetermined", why})` on throw. That preserves the exact "not finding the marker and not being able to look are different answers" semantics.

So the fix:

```ts
// --paginate, because ... (keep the existing comment)
// The bodies come back as a list, not a joined string: the marker is matched with
// a prose-only read per body, so a comment quoting the marker inside a fenced
// sample does not answer for it (#304) — and so an unclosed fence in one comment
// cannot swallow the next comment's marker.
let comments: { body?: string }[];
try {
  comments = ghPaginated<{ body?: string }>(
    "api", `repos/${opts.repo}/issues/${opts.parent}/comments`,
  );
